  const token = req.headers.authorization?.replace(/^Bearer\s+/i, '');
  if (!token) return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Unauthenticated' });
  try {
    req.user = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);
    next();
  } catch {
    res.status(401).json({ error: 'Invalid token' });
  }
}
```

Pagination limits response size. Offset pagination uses `page`/`limit` or `skip`/`limit`; cursor pagination uses a stable indexed key and is more efficient for large/changing datasets. Return metadata such as next cursor or total when appropriate.

```javascript
const page = Math.max(1, Number(req.query.page) || 1);
const limit = Math.min(100, Math.max(1, Number(req.query.limit) || 20));
const items = await Product.find(filter).skip((page - 1) * limit).limit(limit);
```

`find(filter)` returns matching documents; an empty filter matches all documents. Use operators such as `$gt`, `$in`, and `$exists`, and combine filters carefully. Example: `db.users.find({age: {$gte: 18}})`.

```javascript
